  "visual_categories": [
    {
      "category": 1,
      "name": "Scale, layout and route readability",
      "score": 76,
      "evidence": "Yellow floor route and broad central path are easy to find in C01 and cutaways. PLAYER_REVERSE has the thick black scanner beam across the upper view, a post through the lane, and cart-gate panels plus a foreground column over the equipment. PLAYER_PINCH shows the equipment-side view bounded by the arrival door and another column."
    },
    {
      "category": 2,
      "name": "Grounded stylized shape language and object-specific construction",
      "score": 67,
      "evidence": "Dominant objects rely on repeated rectangular masses and shallow bevels: scanner arch/posts (C01, C02, HERO_SCANNER), cart-gate panels (C06), arrival doors (C09), cargo tunnel (C05, HERO_CARGO), office desk (C07), and electrical cabinets (HERO_UTILITIES). Several hero forms lack visible construction logic or distinctive secondary shape."
    },
    {
      "category": 3,
      "name": "Inspection/check-in hero hierarchy and functional composition",
      "score": 72,
      "evidence": "Scanner is prominent in C01, C02 and HERO_SCANNER; the conveyor/crate reads as cargo inspection in C05 and HERO_CARGO. The scanner, cargo system and check-in hatch rarely form one legible sequence. C03 is a close crop with the counter face consuming most of the lower frame; player views show equipment occlusion."
    },
    {
      "category": 4,
      "name": "Tactile material identity and UV/texture discipline",
      "score": 69,
      "evidence": "Neutral views distinguish blue painted cabinets, pale housings, dark metal and floor. Beauty views often share a smooth satin response, especially scanner and panels. UV-standard C05 shows inconsistent checker size/distortion on tunnel/crate; C07 on chair/table edges; HERO_TROLLEY on covered cloth; HERO_UTILITIES on utility tank and service supports. The trolley cloth reads as smooth molded shell rather than fabric."
    },
    {
      "category": 5,
      "name": "Localized lighting, depth and bleak atmosphere",
      "score": 64,
      "evidence": "Practical fixtures and task pools are visible; C03 has a readable warm counter pool. Secondary bays and lower equipment fall near-black in C01, C02 and C05; C07 office window/back wall are dark; C10 is dominated by a nearly black roof grid. Light pools and falloff do not consistently reveal form."
    },
    {
      "category": 6,
      "name": "Approved spawn colour coherence and restrained accents",
      "score": 84,
      "evidence": "Muted peach/pink wall, blue-black lower wall, navy cabinets and restrained orange/yellow accents connect to approved spawn references. C01 yellow route markings and orange scanner header have information value. Large nearly black equipment/ceiling mass compresses the palette."
    },
    {
      "category": 7,
      "name": "Purposeful worker traces and coercive institutional storytelling",
      "score": 73,
      "evidence": "“WE VALUE YOUR TIME / ALL DELAYS ARE YOUR RESPONSIBILITY” is legible in WALL_OFFICE_FRONT; “DO NOT RELEASE” and a custody tag appear in HERO_EVIDENCE; papers, stamp and tray give procedural use in DETAIL_CHECKIN; C05 has a sector custody label. Cues are scattered and small. Wide shots show few human traces, little repair/route wear beyond painted markings, and no visible PPE/work evidence."
    }
  ],
